# Card 6b03ebf0d602a48e11939bbe -- LANDAS binlog DDL watcher.
#
# The binlog already records every destructive DDL with a timestamp and a
# thread_id; this job reads it and shouts when something touches
# super_landas. It runs as root because the binlogs are 0640 root:mysql.
# It NEVER deletes a binlog: retention is Cyd's decision.
#
# 00:10 UTC daily -- after the binlog rotates at midnight, before the nightly
# backup at 19:00 UTC is disturbed. Output is appended, capped by logrotate.
#
# The trail lives in /var/log/landas/, NOT /var/log/mysql/, because the stock
# /etc/logrotate.d/mysql-server globs /var/log/mysql/*log. A file there is
# claimed by two stanzas, logrotate raises "duplicate log entry" and SKIPS the
# whole mysql-server file -- which is what rotates error.log. Keeping our log
# out of that glob keeps that rule alive (card 6b03ebf0d602a48e11939bbe, QA #7).
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
10 0 * * * root /usr/local/bin/landas-ddl-audit --lookback 26 >> /var/log/landas/ddl-audit.log 2>&1
